Moss iOS — experimental native Swift port, 2026.

The inference implementation is a Swift adaptation of MOSS-Image and the
moss-image-mlx reference port. It is not an official OpenMOSS product.

MOSS-Image: OpenMOSS-Team / OpenMOSS contributors, Apache License 2.0.
https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-Base
https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image

MLX reference port: felix-ab/moss-image-mlx, Apache License 2.0.
https://github.com/felix-ab/moss-image-mlx
Includes the decoder strip strategy, scheduler convention, precision handling,
and CPU noise convention also attributed there to felix-ab/flux3-mlx.

MLX Swift: Copyright Apple Inc., MIT License.
https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-swift
The build obtains MLX Swift and its dependencies from their upstream packages;
their licenses and notices remain applicable. See Licenses/.

Model exports: VisualInference/MOSS-Image-Base-MLX-8bit and
VisualInference/MOSS-Image-SFT-MLX-compact, Apache License 2.0.
8-step adapter: lodestones/MOSS-Image-Base-8-steps-dmd, Apache License 2.0.
Model file revisions and SHA-256 hashes are in Moss/Resources/model-manifest.json.

Changes in this project: SwiftUI iOS interface, a streamed Swift tensor reader,
Swift implementations of the text encoder, transformer, scheduler and VAE,
iOS download and gallery services, build automation, and original icon artwork.
Quantization and streamed evaluation can change numerical results; output parity
with the original PyTorch pipeline has not been established on iPhone.
